# Git rewrites LF to CRLF on Windows checkout by default, which changes the
# bytes of every file and therefore every published MD5. A reader cloning on
# Windows would get raw.csv at 4c0038e9f569bfe6e199116f6469732d instead of
# 7b68a001709821c71ece5b8ed209d4d3 and reasonably conclude the data had been
# altered. These patterns match at any depth, subdirectories included.
*.csv -text
*.svg -text
*.md  -text
*.py  -text
